    {
      "n": 2,
      "title": "Enzyme Function & Factors Affecting Activity",
      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-II-i-j-17",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Explain how enzymes catalyze reactions.</li><li>Describe factors affecting enzyme activity.</li><li>Explain denaturation.</li><li>Interpret enzyme activity graphs.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Activation energy</strong> — energy needed to start a reaction.</li><li><strong>Denaturation</strong> — loss of enzyme shape and function.</li><li><strong>Optimal pH/temperature</strong> — conditions where enzyme works best.</li><li><strong>Inhibitor</strong> — molecule that slows/prevents enzyme action.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. How Enzymes Work</h4><p>Enzymes lower activation energy by bringing substrates together in the correct orientation. The enzyme is not consumed.</p><h4>B. Factors Affecting Enzyme Activity</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Temperature</td><td>Activity increases until optimum, then denatures</td></tr><tr><td>pH</td><td>Each enzyme has an optimal pH</td></tr><tr><td>Substrate concentration</td><td>Rate increases until saturation</td></tr><tr><td>Enzyme concentration</td><td>Rate increases with more enzyme</td></tr><tr><td>Inhibitors</td><td>Reduce or block activity</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>C. Types of Inhibition</h4><ul><li><strong>Competitive</strong> — inhibitor binds active site</li><li><strong>Non-competitive</strong> — inhibitor binds elsewhere, changes shape</li></ul>",
      "activity1": {
        "timeLimit": 90,
        "badgeId": "activity-master",
        "badgeName": "Activity Master",
        "badgeIcon": "📈",
        "pairs": [
          { "key": "ae", "left": "Activation energy", "right": "Energy needed to start reaction" },
          { "key": "denat", "left": "Denaturation", "right": "Loss of enzyme shape" },
