      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-II-i-j-18",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Explain redox in respiration and photosynthesis.</li><li>Describe how electron transport chains work.</li><li>Relate redox to energy production.</li><li>Identify examples of redox in daily life.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Electron transport chain (ETC)</strong> — series of redox reactions producing ATP.</li><li><strong>Oxidative phosphorylation</strong> — ATP production using ETC in respiration.</li><li><strong>Photophosphorylation</strong> — ATP production using ETC in photosynthesis.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Redox in Cellular Respiration</h4><ul><li>Glucose is oxidized → CO₂</li><li>O₂ is reduced → H₂O</li><li>Electrons carried by NADH/FADH₂ to the ETC</li><li>ATP produced by chemiosmosis</li></ul><h4>B. Redox in Photosynthesis</h4><ul><li>H₂O is oxidized → O₂</li><li>CO₂ is reduced → glucose</li><li>Electrons carried by NADPH</li><li>ATP produced by photophosphorylation</li></ul><h4>C. Everyday Redox</h4><ul><li>Rusting of iron (oxidation)</li><li>Burning of fuel (oxidation)</li><li>Batteries (electron flow)</li><li>Bleaching (oxidation of pigments)</li></ul>",
